file: "packages/editor/src/gestures/commands.ts"
doc: "The command registry every chord, island button, palette row and menu row dispatches through."

structs: [
  { name: "Command"
    change_type: MODIFIED
    doc:
      "Gains one optional field, `appliesTo`. `id`, `label` and `run` are\n"
      "unchanged.\n"
      "\n"
      "POINTER SURFACE means, precisely, the two surfaces that BUILD their\n"
      "rows by walking this registry: the command palette and the context\n"
      "menu. It does not mean the islands or the toolbar -- those hard-code\n"
      "the handful of buttons they show and consult no field here, so\n"
      "nothing in this doc constrains them.\n"
      "\n"
      "The field carries two separable facts, and the two surfaces read\n"
      "different amounts of it:\n"
      "\n"
      "  PRESENT or ABSENT -- read by BOTH surfaces. Absent means keyboard\n"
      "  only: the command appears on neither.\n"
      "\n"
      "  THE VALUE, when present -- read by the CONTEXT MENU ONLY.\n"
      "    'global'     offer whatever is selected, including nothing.\n"
      "    a kind list  offer only when the selection is non-empty and at\n"
      "                 least one selected element's kind is in the list.\n"
      "\n"
      "  The palette ignores the value entirely and offers every command\n"
      "  that has one, because it is reached by a chord with no pointer\n"
      "  context and is a search over everything the editor can do. So `hide`\n"
      "  is listed in the palette with nothing selected, and absent from the\n"
      "  menu until a node is. commandPaletteItems states the same split from\n"
      "  its side.\n"
      "\n"
      "  'global' therefore means 'not filtered BY SELECTION' rather than\n"
      "  'shown everywhere unconditionally'. A surface may still drop a\n"
      "  'global' command for a reason of its own -- the palette drops\n"
      "  'open-palette', because a row reopening the palette you are in is\n"
      "  dead -- and that is not a contradiction of this field.\n"
      "\n"
      "OPT-IN, NOT OPT-OUT, and that direction is the point. A command added\n"
      "later with no `appliesTo` appears on no pointer surface until someone\n"
      "decides it should. The opposite default has already failed here:\n"
      "PALETTE_EXCLUDED was an exclusion list, and adding two commands to the\n"
      "registry silently made it stale.\n"
      "\n"
      "A single kind is still a list -- ['node'], not 'node' -- because\n"
      "reset-size genuinely needs three, and one shape for the list case is\n"
      "worth more than the brevity."
    fields: [
      { name: "id",        type: { named: { symbol: "CommandId" } } },
      { name: "label",     type: { primitive: CHARACTER } },
      { name: "run",       type: { arrow: { inputs: [{ named: { symbol: "CommandContext" } }], output: { primitive: VOID } } } },
      { name: "appliesTo", type: { unsupported: { reason: UNION_AT_TYPE_POSITION, source_excerpt: "'global' | Array<ElementKind>" } }, is_optional: true }
    ]
    typescript: { struct_kind: STRUCT_KIND_INTERFACE }
  }
]

constants: [
  { name: "COMMANDS"
    change_type: MODIFIED
    doc:
      "No entry is added, removed or reordered, and no `run` body changes.\n"
      "Twenty-three of the thirty-two entries gain an `appliesTo`; the other\n"
      "nine deliberately get none.\n"
      "\n"
      "'global' -- seventeen: undo, redo, select-all, save, auto-layout,\n"
      "pin-all, unpin-all, add-annotation, open-palette, open-help,\n"
      "tool-select, tool-hand, tool-annotation, zoom-in, zoom-out,\n"
      "zoom-reset, zoom-fit.\n"
      "\n"
      "Kind lists -- six:\n"
      "  delete          ['annotation']  D3: Delete is annotations-only, and\n"
      "                                  runDelete already skips every other\n"
      "                                  kind. Offering it on a node would\n"
      "                                  advertise a no-op.\n"
      "  edit-text       ['annotation']  runEditText requires exactly one\n"
      "                                  annotation.\n"
      "  duplicate       ['annotation']  runDuplicate skips non-annotations.\n"
      "  hide            ['node']        runHide filters to node ids.\n"
      "  reset-size      ['node', 'group', 'annotation']  every kind that\n"
      "                                  carries a size. Not edges.\n"
      "  focus-inspector ['node', 'edge', 'group', 'annotation']  the\n"
      "                                  inspector shows the selection, so\n"
      "                                  any selection is meaningful and an\n"
      "                                  empty one is not.\n"
      "\n"
      "Absent -- nine: nudge-up, nudge-down, nudge-left, nudge-right,\n"
      "ring-next, ring-prev, escape, enter-grab, enter-resize.\n"
      "\n"
      "Each of those nine needs a keyboard to mean anything. The nudge and\n"
      "ring commands are built to repeat under a held key, and one click of\n"
      "'Nudge up' moves a selection one pixel. 'escape' is contextual --\n"
      "close an overlay, else clear the selection -- and a row that does one\n"
      "of two things depending on hidden state is not a row. enter-grab and\n"
      "enter-resize open a mode whose next keystrokes are the feature, which\n"
      "is precisely what a user who just reached for the mouse does not have\n"
      "their hands positioned for.\n"
      "\n"
      "A GAP THIS SURFACE MAKES VISIBLE, and does not close. D3 and 11.4 of\n"
      "docs/editor-ui-review.md both say Contract (group) belongs in the\n"
      "palette and the context menu beside Hide. There is no `contract`\n"
      "command in this registry and this pillar adds none -- collapsing a\n"
      "group is a real feature with its own semantics, not a menu concern. So\n"
      "a right-click on a group offers the globals plus reset-size and\n"
      "focus-inspector, and nothing group-specific. That is the first place\n"
      "the promise is visibly unmet; it is noted here rather than left for\n"
      "the next reader to rediscover.\n"
      "\n"
      "The kind lists above are each narrower than the command's own guard,\n"
      "on purpose: runDelete already ignores a node, so nothing breaks if it\n"
      "is dispatched by chord on one. `appliesTo` decides what is OFFERED,\n"
      "never what is permitted, and no `run` body should start checking it."
    type: { named: { symbol: "Array", args: [{ named: { symbol: "Command" } }] } }
    uses: ["CommandContext", "ElementKind"]
  }
]
